      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That's probably not a bad muscle pull, but rather a minor strain on your lower back. The pain shooting down into your stomach is likely due to the referred pain from the sciatic nerve. I recommend taking a few ibuprofen, but make sure to take it with a glass of water and a pinch of salt to help reduce inflammation. You should also try to stretch it out with some gentle yoga poses, like downward-facing dog or child's pose, to help alleviate the discomfort.",
